{
  "format": 1,
  "metadata": {
    "kernelspec": {
      "name": "affon",
      "display_name": "Affon (TypeScript)",
      "language": "typescript"
    }
  },
  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "cell-1",
      "kind": "markdown",
      "language": "markdown",
      "source": "# Illustrated Losses And Metrics\n\nA loss is optimized during training. A metric is reported to describe quality. Losses return tensors and can participate in gradients; metrics return JavaScript numbers.\n\nUse the learning loop here too: predict what a perfect prediction would score, run the example, then interpret whether bigger or smaller is better.\n",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "cell-2",
      "kind": "code",
      "language": "typescript",
      "source": "import { tensor, accuracy, precision, recall, f1, mse, mae, r2 } from 'affon:compute'\nimport nn from 'affon:nn'\n\nfunction show(label: string, value: { shape: readonly number[], to_array(): unknown }) {\n  console.log(label)\n  console.log('shape:', value.shape)\n  console.log(JSON.stringify(value.to_array()))\n}\n",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "cell-3",
      "kind": "markdown",
      "language": "markdown",
      "source": "## Regression Losses And Metrics\n\n$$\n\\mathrm{MSE}=\\frac{1}{N}\\sum_i(\\hat{y}_i-y_i)^2\n$$\n\n$$\n\\mathrm{MAE}=\\frac{1}{N}\\sum_i|\\hat{y}_i-y_i|\n$$\n\n`MSELoss` is the training loss version. `mse` and `mae` are reporting helpers.\n",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "cell-4",
      "kind": "markdown",
      "language": "markdown",
      "source": "### Before You Run\n\nFor predictions `[2, 4]` and targets `[1, 5]`, each error has magnitude `1`. Predict MSE and MAE before running.\n\n### Read The Output\n\nMSE and MAE are both `1` here because both mistakes have absolute error `1`; squaring does not change them.\n",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "cell-5",
      "kind": "code",
      "language": "typescript",
      "source": "const pred = tensor([2, 4])\nconst target = tensor([1, 5])\nconst mseLoss = nn.MSELoss()\nshow('MSELoss(pred, target)', mseLoss(pred, target))\nconsole.log('mse:', mse(pred, target))\nconsole.log('mae:', mae(pred, target))\nconsole.log('r2:', r2(pred, target))\n",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "cell-6",
      "kind": "markdown",
      "language": "markdown",
      "source": "## Binary Losses\n\n`BCELoss` expects probability-like predictions. `BCEWithLogitsLoss` expects raw logits and applies the sigmoid-style conversion internally.\n\n```txt\nprobability -> BCELoss\nlogit       -> BCEWithLogitsLoss\n```\n",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "cell-7",
      "kind": "markdown",
      "language": "markdown",
      "source": "### Before You Run\n\nAsk which input is already probability-like and which input is a raw logit. That decides whether to use `BCELoss` or `BCEWithLogitsLoss`.\n",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "cell-8",
      "kind": "code",
      "language": "typescript",
      "source": "const binaryTarget = tensor([1, 0, 1])\nshow('BCELoss probabilities', nn.BCELoss()(tensor([0.9, 0.2, 0.7]), binaryTarget))\nshow('BCEWithLogitsLoss logits', nn.BCEWithLogitsLoss()(tensor([2, -1, 1]), binaryTarget))\n",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "cell-9",
      "kind": "markdown",
      "language": "markdown",
      "source": "## Cross Entropy\n\nCross entropy compares class logits against target class labels.\n\n```txt\nlogits: [batch, classes]\ntarget: [batch]\nloss:   [1]\n```\n\nIt rewards high score on the correct class and penalizes high scores on wrong classes.\n",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "cell-10",
      "kind": "markdown",
      "language": "markdown",
      "source": "### Before You Run\n\nFor each row of logits, identify the largest class score. If it matches the target class, the loss should be relatively small.\n",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "cell-11",
      "kind": "code",
      "language": "typescript",
      "source": "const logits = tensor([[2, 1, 0], [0, 3, 1]])\nconst classes = tensor([0, 1], { dtype: 'i64' })\nshow('CrossEntropyLoss(logits, classes)', nn.CrossEntropyLoss()(logits, classes))\n",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "cell-12",
      "kind": "markdown",
      "language": "markdown",
      "source": "## Classification Metrics\n\nClassification metrics are easiest to read through a confusion matrix.\n\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 560 250\" width=\"560\" height=\"250\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n  <style>.txt{font:14px sans-serif;fill:#0f172a}.mono{font:16px monospace}.h{fill:#dbeafe;stroke:#60a5fa}.good{fill:#dcfce7;stroke:#4ade80}.bad{fill:#fee2e2;stroke:#f87171}</style>\n  <text class=\"txt\" x=\"210\" y=\"30\">actual</text><text class=\"txt\" x=\"25\" y=\"125\">predicted</text>\n  <rect class=\"h\" x=\"170\" y=\"55\" width=\"130\" height=\"40\"/><text class=\"mono\" x=\"220\" y=\"80\">yes</text>\n  <rect class=\"h\" x=\"300\" y=\"55\" width=\"130\" height=\"40\"/><text class=\"mono\" x=\"350\" y=\"80\">no</text>\n  <rect class=\"h\" x=\"80\" y=\"95\" width=\"90\" height=\"55\"/><text class=\"mono\" x=\"108\" y=\"128\">yes</text>\n  <rect class=\"h\" x=\"80\" y=\"150\" width=\"90\" height=\"55\"/><text class=\"mono\" x=\"112\" y=\"183\">no</text>\n  <rect class=\"good\" x=\"170\" y=\"95\" width=\"130\" height=\"55\"/><text class=\"mono\" x=\"222\" y=\"128\">TP</text>\n  <rect class=\"bad\" x=\"300\" y=\"95\" width=\"130\" height=\"55\"/><text class=\"mono\" x=\"352\" y=\"128\">FP</text>\n  <rect class=\"bad\" x=\"170\" y=\"150\" width=\"130\" height=\"55\"/><text class=\"mono\" x=\"222\" y=\"183\">FN</text>\n  <rect class=\"good\" x=\"300\" y=\"150\" width=\"130\" height=\"55\"/><text class=\"mono\" x=\"352\" y=\"183\">TN</text>\n</svg>\n\n$$\nprecision = \\frac{TP}{TP+FP},\\quad recall = \\frac{TP}{TP+FN}\n$$\n",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "cell-13",
      "kind": "markdown",
      "language": "markdown",
      "source": "### Before You Run\n\nThreshold the binary predictions at `0.5`. Count TP, FP, FN, and TN by hand, then compare with precision, recall, and F1.\n\n### Debugging Cue\n\nIf accuracy looks good but precision or recall looks bad, inspect the confusion matrix. Accuracy can hide class imbalance.\n",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "cell-14",
      "kind": "code",
      "language": "typescript",
      "source": "const binPred = tensor([0.9, 0.2, 0.8, 0.4])\nconst binTarget = tensor([1, 0, 0, 1])\nconsole.log('precision:', precision(binPred, binTarget))\nconsole.log('recall:', recall(binPred, binTarget))\nconsole.log('f1:', f1(binPred, binTarget))\nconsole.log('multiclass accuracy:', accuracy(logits, classes))\n",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {}
    }
  ]
}
